{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546274-wi-necromancer-revenants","id":1546274,"title":"WI: Necromancer Revenants","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-21T20:57:47-08:00","id":1546274,"title":"WI: Necromancer Revenants","content":"I\u2019ve long thought it would be cool if some of the families associated with the Giovanni were Revenant families. For the Giovanni themselves, it makes perfect sense because they are already an insular inbred family who frequently become ghouls. <br /> <br /> The Rossellini were turned into canon Revenants. The Dunsirn family also seem like natural Revenants with their twisted practices. They could also have the Nagaraja flaw.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t necessarily mean that these families have to serve Clan Giovanni. In a 5th edition game they could be in service to the Hecata Clan. In a Dark Ages (or an alternative setting where the Cappadocian never fell) game, they could be servants of the Cappadocian Clan. It seems like the Cappadocians would benefit a lot from Revenant families who could handle politics, finance, and social situations for a Clan that is more focused on mysticism. <br /> <br /> What does everybody think of this idea and how would it change the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-22T20:35:56-08:00","id":1546298,"title":"","content":"Honestly of all of the current vampire clans, I always found it a bit weird that the Giovanni didn't have a strong Revenant family or two. Being weird, magically inclined insular, incestuous vampires is kind of their thing and that's exactly what you'd expect to give rise to a family of Revenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-23T08:53:32-08:00","id":1546306,"title":"","content":"Revenants tend to be horribly psychologically broken and tormented people, generally not functional in any genuine social capacity. Not like &quot;slightly weird but okay whatever&quot;, but like &quot;hannibal lecter&quot; or &quot;jeffrey epstein&quot;. The most functional revenant families are the Grimaldi and Zantosa, and frankly, that speaks for itself.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much the opposite of what the Giovanni actually need, given their financial, crime, and political connections, and their use of mortal family members to manage them. The proxy kiss alone (by way of ghoulification) already compromises family members' ability to interact outside the family, and Puttanesca alone are bad enough for the clan's image; revenants would be simply unmanageable and too high-risk to put in the positions Giovanni expect of their mortals.<br /> <br /> Moreover, mortal family members can still practice necromancy, by way of hedge sorcery. They dont strictly need the blood to ply their real trade.<br /> <br /> So, it's impractical and unnecessary for them to have revenants among them. The risk-reward profile just doesn't add up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-23T13:53:59-08:00","id":1546322,"title":"","content":"Funny that you should mention Hannibal Lecter and Jeffrey Epstein as people who aren\u2019t socially function when both of those guys were highly socially functional and competent. Hannibal Lecter is an almost cartoonishly evil genius who has nearly superhuman insights into human nature and generally succeeds at his plans. Epstein is more realistic because he is, in fact, real. But for years Epstein was a huge power player in politics and rubbed elbows with (an likely controlled) some of the most powerful men in the world - including presidents and billionaires.<br /> <br /> Both of those guys misdeeds caught up with them, but they were highly effective. <br /> <br /> The Revenant families vary in how effective they are at acquiring wealth and power, but it\u2019s suggested that at least the Grimaldi are extremely effective at it. They rule a small country in fact.<br /> <br /> Are Revenants the most effective way to gain wealth and power? No. It\u2019s far more effective just to find normal humans who became rich and powerful on their own and then ghoul them or dominate them. But Revenants are about pure effectiveness, Revenants are a cultural manifestation of certain values. Values that the Giovanni embody.<br /> <br /> If the Giovanni were only interested in attaining power, they wouldn\u2019t be a family at all. They would just embrace the most competent mortals they could find. They certainly wouldn\u2019t practice incest or stay so insular. Yet those are part of their values - they care about their family, they think that their family is special, they want to preserve the unique traits and culture of their family, not simply embrace people for efficiency. All sorts of real world and fictional institutions are motivated less by pure efficiency and more by culture and values.<br /> <br /> It is exactly the attitudes which allow the Giovanni to maintain their existence as a family that would lead to the creation of Revenants. They perfectly which with the theme and flavor of the Giovanni Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T07:18:43-08:00","id":1546337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546274-wi-necromancer-revenants?p=1546306#post1546306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants tend to be horribly psychologically broken and tormented people, generally not functional in any genuine social capacity. Not like &quot;slightly weird but okay whatever&quot;, but like &quot;hannibal lecter&quot; or &quot;jeffrey epstein&quot;. The most functional revenant families are the Grimaldi and Zantosa, and frankly, that speaks for itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>My pick would be Rafastio remnants, who are imo also the most likely to dabble in necromancy. As 'witches for hire', I could easily see them as mercs for the Giovanni. With the caveat that the remaining Rafastio probably still harbor a philosophical stance from their Tal'mahe'ra days which isn't necessarily fully compatible with Giovanni doctrine.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T14:49:59-08:00","id":1546355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546274-wi-necromancer-revenants?p=1546322#post1546322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny that you should mention Hannibal Lecter and Jeffrey Epstein as people who aren\u2019t socially function when both of those guys were highly socially functional and competent. Hannibal Lecter is an almost cartoonishly evil genius who has nearly superhuman insights into human nature and generally succeeds at his plans. Epstein is more realistic because he is, in fact, real. But for years Epstein was a huge power player in politics and rubbed elbows with (an likely controlled) some of the most powerful men in the world - including presidents and billionaires.<br /> <br /> Both of those guys misdeeds caught up with them, but they were highly effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much a case of &quot;don't be fooled by appearances&quot;. Neither of the above-listed examples were socially &quot;functional&quot;, despite appearances.<br /> <br /> It's far better shown in the show than the films, but Lecter wasn't as socially adept as a superficial analysis grants. Few genuinely liked him, and most were put off by him; those who did like him, only liked him on the most superficial levels: they weren't interested in Lecter as a person but rather the utility promised by being in his &quot;circle&quot;. Meanwhile, Lecter was skilled at masking, networking, making himself useful to connected people, identifying risks to himself, and socially isolating and discrediting/implicating those who posed a threat.<br /> <br /> With the benefit of hindsight, Epstein proved himself even less socially adept than Lecter. He was good at branding himself, that's about it. The only people outspoken about his much-lauded &quot;charisma&quot; before or after his misdeeds came to light -- and actually seemed genuine in their praise -- were fellow sociopathic elites enjoying quid-pro-quo relationships, whether that was for financial, social, or less-salacious reasons. They praised him because he was useful to them, and vice versa. For the rest, he was the guy you tolerated because you were expected to tolerate him, if for no reason other to protect your own socioeconomic status.<br /> <br /> Or to put it in gaming terms, he was the metagaming munchkin weirdo everyone else at the table secretly detested, but you had to let him play because he's the one who owned all the books and could host the game. As long as there was no alternative you had to be nice, but once someone else picked up the books or found an alternate place to play, you could curb his ass and everyone could be honest about how big a dick he was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are Revenants the most effective way to gain wealth and power? No... </div> </div> </div>This isn't just about <i>gaining</i> wealth and power. It's about the risk-reward portfolio, cost-benefit analysis, the price of maintenance, and opportunity cost. The Giovanni aren't restrictive and procedural for purely sociocultural reasons; their traditions are best practices to maintain control over mortal family members and their assets. The proxy kiss, for example, would be far less useful as a measure to exercise control if the mortals in their family generated their own vitae, and without invoking the blood bond.<br /> <br /> By contrast, look to the measures the Tzimisce take to keep their revenant families under control, the harm dealt to the clan when one of them slips the leash, and the cost of correcting that error. Measures like them are simply cost-prohibitive for a clan positioned such as the Giovanni, when better alternatives exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Giovanni were only interested in attaining power, they wouldn\u2019t be a family at all... </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni <i>do</i> reproduce, marry, and even embrace outside the (immediate) family. If they didn't, the Pisanob, Dunsirn, Milliner, Puttanesca, Rosselini, and the other satellite families wouldn't exist. Moreover, the Giovanni themselves aren't a single mortal lineage, but a network of interconnected lineages that surround a central &quot;trunk&quot; descended directly from Augustus. In fact, the Giovanni specifically forbid embraces from within one's immediate or proximal mortal family; when the anziani negotiate and approve an embrace, the job's given to an approved sire from distal family at best, but most commonly a different lineage entirely.<br /> <br /> Hell if I remember right, there's even a canon character who's not even a Giovanni by blood, but rather a promising (but completely unrelated) mortal who married in to later earn the proxy kiss and embrace...specifically as a Giovanni, as opposed to being assigned satellite family membership for which this was the norm. Damned if I remember which one, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...They certainly wouldn\u2019t practice incest or stay so insular... </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the Tzimisce...<br /> <br /> The typical perception of who the Giovanni are and what they do is more appropriately attributed to pre-modern Tzimisce from which the revenant families originate. That is to say, discrete and nuclear families that exclusively inbreed -- as in sibling, parent/child, aunt/nephew and uncle/niece, first and second cousin shit -- that create a family tree that doesn't branch but rather loop back in on itself.<br /> <br /> While that does happen with the Giovanni, it's not the norm -- most &quot;incest&quot; as practiced by the Giovanni is only such in the most liberal interpretation of the word. More to the point, the majority of it is between distantly-related family, in-laws, and the like. Not closely enough to risk congenital problems, and distant enough to be legal (if not necessarily moral) in the majority of the world. Remember that as I said, the Giovanni family is quite large -- large enough to &quot;keep it in the family&quot; without risking &quot;banjo music&quot; scenarios, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T10:54:06-08:00","id":1546397,"title":"","content":"We may not see eye to eye here, but what if the Cappadocians created these Revenant families, including the Giovanni?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}